    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17209" root="ريأ" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِىْءٌ</span></b>  a subst. from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَآءَ</span> mentioned above: (M,
K:) [i. e., it signifies <i>Sight;</i> &amp;c.; like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُؤْيَةٌ</span>:]
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَآءٌ</span> is said by MF to be like it; but this is a
mistake, occasioned by his finding <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الرَّآء</span>, in a verse,
miswritten for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الدَّآء</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِئْى</span>.]

